-- title:
--   Valuation dichotomy in the localised modular presentation ring
-- statement:
--   Let $L$ be a field, $A \subseteq L$ a valuation subring, $k$ a field and $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$ a ring homomorphism (no surjectivity is required), and let $N$ be a nonzero natural number. Assume given `data : ModularPolynomialData N`, that is a monic $\Phi \in (\mathbb{Z}[X])[Y]$ of $Y$-degree $\psi(N) =$ `dedekindPsi N` $= \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$ which vanishes when $X$ is evaluated at the $q$-expansion $j(q)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and $Y$ at $j(q^N)$. Assume further the degree hypothesis `hdeg`: inside the field of Laurent series over $k$, the relative rank of $k(\,\overline{j}\,) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin k {jqModC k}` in `modularFunctionFieldC k N` $= k(\overline{j}, \overline{j}_N)$ equals $\psi(N)$, where `jqModC k` is the $q$-expansion $q^{-1}(E_4^3 \cdot \eta\text{-unit}^{-1})$ of $j$ with coefficients in $k$ and `jqNModC k N` is its image under $q \mapsto q^N$. Then for every Laurent series $f$ over $L$ lying in $L(j, j_N) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin L {jqModC L, jqNModC L N}`, either $f$ or $f^{-1}$ lies in `modularLocalized N A.toSubring red`, the subring of those $g$ with $g s = r$ for some $r, s$ in the subring $R$ of $L((q))$ generated by the constant series with coefficients in $A$ together with $j$ and $j_N$, with $s$ outside the prime ideal `redKer` of $R$ attached to `red`.
--
--   This is the dichotomy statement asserting that the localisation of $A[j, j_N]$ at the reduction prime determined by `red` exhausts, up to inversion, the whole two-generator modular function field over $L$; it plays the role of a valuation-theoretic covering property at the modular site of level $N$. It is used in the treatment of place specialisations and prolongation tuples, for instance in the cusp law at infinity, the construction of a finite order subalgebra spanning the relevant module, and the norm-reduction estimate.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPReduction_mem_or_inv_mem_modularLocalized.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_CharPReduction
import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X0
import Mathlib.FieldTheory.Relrank

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
